/* STDLIB/iii/aether/tomeus.iii -- ΤΟΜΕΥΣ, THE CUTTER: THE EXACT SPECTRUM OF THE HINGE, AND THE GAP READ WHOLE.
 *   Page first: DOCS/III-TOMEUS-THE-CUTTER-PREREGISTRATION.md (8cd2e9f76, 2026-10-27 05:2x).  Composes ΣΤΡΟΦΙΓΞ (the blocks of the
 *   transfer matrix of Z2 / S3 / Q8 lattice gauge theory on 2x2xL, handed over modulo any prime through sfx_wblockfill), ΜΕΓΕΘΟΣ
 *   (every big integer), and as the second road ΧΑΡΑΚΤΗΡ and sturm_big on the blocks their envelope admits.
 *   THE OBJECT.  For a block B (rows the S-orbit representatives of one (e, k) sector, W-even or W-odd where the sector is W-stable)
 *   the characteristic polynomial P(x) = det(xI - B) in Z[x], EXACT: modulo each of a list of verified primes below 2^30 by a
 *   Hessenberg reduction with pivoting and the Hessenberg recurrence (O(n^3) per prime), the number of primes sized to EXCEED the
 *   coefficient bound n (rowbits + 1) + 64 bits (|c_k| <= C(n,k) lambda_0^k and lambda_0 <= the infinity norm < 2^rowbits) before any
 *   reconstruction, Garner through ΜΕΓΕΘΟΣ into the organ's own limb images, centred.  THE CERTIFICATE: every block is similar to a
 *   symmetric positive-semidefinite matrix (Osterwalder-Seiler), so every root is real and nonnegative; Descartes' count V of the
 *   coefficient signs must equal n - m0 (m0 the multiplicity of the root 0), which forces exactly n - m0 positive roots -- read on every
 *   block (law 4: a count that falls short accuses the instrument).  THE ROOTS: the largest root of P (and of P', P'', ... where the
 *   second root is wanted) bracketed by Newton from above on dyadics m/2^32 -- for a real-rooted polynomial Newton from above the largest
 *   root stays above it and decreases, each iterate rounded UP, the bracket closed when P(m - 1) < 0; the second root by bisection on
 *   the sign of P between the largest root of P'' (or P''', when P'' sits above it) and the largest root of P', then CERTIFIED by two
 *   Budan-Fourier counts (the sign changes of the Taylor coefficients at a dyadic point, exact on a real-rooted polynomial): exactly two
 *   roots above the lower end, exactly one above the upper; a failed certificate falls back to a count bisection.  THE READINGS: lambda_0
 *   from the trivial block (Perron-Frobenius: M is entrywise positive, its Perron vector S-invariant), lambda_1 the largest among the
 *   vacuum sector's other roots with its (k, w), lambda_e the largest root of each electric sector with its (k, w); the gap and the string
 *   energies are the logarithms of the ratios of these brackets, taken at the desk.  THE ROADS: Newton's identities turn P into the power
 *   sums p_1..p_6, which must equal ΣΤΡΟΦΙΓΞ's traces of the same block by matrix squaring; ΧΑΡΑΚΤΗΡ's charpoly must equal P coefficient
 *   for coefficient where its envelope admits the block (n <= 64, entries <= 2^20), and sturm_big must count one root in the bracket.
 *   W = 0 for every technique; the exact spectra, gaps and energies are III's.  The functions are kept small (the compiler's 64-slot wall). */
module aether_tomeus

extern @abi(c-msvc-x64) fn krx_s(s: u64) -> u64 from "keryx.iii"
extern @abi(c-msvc-x64) fn krx_u(v: u64) -> u64 from "keryx.iii"
extern @abi(c-msvc-x64) fn krx_nl() -> u64 from "keryx.iii"
extern @abi(c-msvc-x64) fn mgs_setu(r: u64, v: u64) -> u64 from "megethos.iii"
extern @abi(c-msvc-x64) fn mgs_zero(r: u64) -> u64 from "megethos.iii"
extern @abi(c-msvc-x64) fn mgs_add(d: u64, a: u64, b: u64) -> u64 from "megethos.iii"
extern @abi(c-msvc-x64) fn mgs_sub(d: u64, a: u64, b: u64) -> u64 from "megethos.iii"
extern @abi(c-msvc-x64) fn mgs_mul(d: u64, a: u64, b: u64) -> u64 from "megethos.iii"
extern @abi(c-msvc-x64) fn mgs_divmod(q: u64, r: u64, a: u64, b: u64) -> u64 from "megethos.iii"
extern @abi(c-msvc-x64) fn mgs_copy(d: u64, s: u64) -> u64 from "megethos.iii"
